<p>To protect your vehicle during transportation, it is highly recommended to opt for insurance coverage. The declared-value transit marine insurance is a common type provided by car transport companies. Here's a breakdown of the estimated premiums:</p>

<h3>Declared-Value Transit Marine Insurance</h3>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Insurance Premium:</strong> The premium amount varies depending on the declared value of your car, the insurance company providing the coverage, and the type of insurance policy you choose (e.g., comprehensive, third-party). However, as an approximate guide, you can expect to pay around <span style="font-weight:bold;">₹200 - 500</span> per <span style="font-weight:bold;">₹1 lakh</span> declared value.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Declared-Value:</strong> You are required to declare the current market value of your car before transportation. If the declared value is higher than the actual value, you will be responsible for any loss above the declared value during transportation.</span></li>
</ul>

<h3>Claim Protections</h3>
<p>Car transport companies often provide claim protection plans to cover potential losses during transportation. These plans can include:</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Actual Cash Value (ACV) Insurance:</strong> This plan covers the actual value of your car rather than the declared value. If the vehicle is damaged or lost during transportation, a certain percentage (e.g., 80%) of the ACV will be paid as compensation.</span></li>
    <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Agreed Value Insurance:</strong> Similar to ACV, agreed value insurance also covers the actual value of your car. However, the agreed value is determined beforehand by both you and the transport company. In case of damage or loss, you will be compensated based on the agreed value.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Please note that the specific terms and conditions of claim protections may vary between car transport companies. It is essential to discuss these options with the transport company and understand the implications before making a choice.</p></div>
